ently on lisinopril… held since Sep 29 for soft BP')"},"testCase":{"id":"dda95ed859f3d63b458277927abab2b3","externalId":"c629c955d1899fef7b2d01e32fca6414","name":"[dev] S07 Typed medication questions with one right answer: why held, held now, stopped, given once (Hospital; NH variants)","fullName":"TC-15 Ask AI › TC-15/S07"},"descriptionHtml":"<p><b>Case priority: P0 · stated in the UAT / ticket AC</b> · TFA-92593 AC 5, AC 7 · “Free-form typed/dictated questions are also answered correctly”.</p><div class=\"rc-approach\"><p><b>Approach</b> · TC-15 Ask AI · <b>S07</b> Typed medication questions with one right answer: why held, held now, stopped, given once (Hospital; NH variants)</p><p><b>UAT steps / ticket ACs covered:</b></p><ul><li><b>U2</b> A typed custom question is answered correctly. (UAT TC-15; TFA-92593 AC 5)</li><li><b>U5</b> The current-medications answer reflects the Medication Tracker; held drugs show as held. (UAT TC-15; TFA-92593 AC 7)</li><li><b>U4</b> Answers are grounded only in that patient's data: no cross-patient bleed, no invented information, no outside data; per 3.4 no guessed units on ambiguous values and no narration of documentation stat … (UAT TC-15; TFA-92593 AC 3; UAT 3.4)</li></ul><p><b>Test design technique: </b>Equivalence classes (equivalence) — Check the same rule again with another class of input (Hospital / Nursing Home, other data); every class has to be right.</p><p><b>Given </b>Tracker with one row per status class: active, held (soft BP), discontinued, one-time dose</p><p><b>When </b>Type &quot;Why is the lisinopril held?&quot;; variants type the status questions, in both modes</p><p><b>Then </b>The stored reason is given; held reads as held, stopped as stopped, the one-time dose as given once</p><p><b>Pass rule (oracle, excerpt): </b>Main: mustInclude BP / blood pressure / hypotension, no other reason (U2, U4). Variants: lisinopril → 'held|on hold'; enoxaparin → 'stopped|discontinued|no longer'; ondansetron → 'once|one-time|single'. A stopped drug presented as current is a Fail whatever Q3 decides</p><p><b>Where it ran: </b>dev unit U36; test method AICHECK · AI output check; lane planned in the matrix: AI check (automated)</p><p><small>S07 is our own case number (its number in the coverage matrix cases/TC-15.matrix.json), not a step number of the UAT document.</small></p></div><p><b>Environment: dev</b> — dev deployment, build <code>8b4be94</code> (Deploy Convex, 2026-10-19T17:04:37Z); account and address are not written into the report; run folder <code>runs/2026-10-14-dev</code>.</p><p><b>Test method:</b> AICHECK · AI output check; secondary: AGENT · Browser agent — as classified in cases/test-methods.json, which says it runs on both; Source: <code>dev</code>.</p><p><b>UAT item:</b> TC-15 Ask AI · <b>Section:</b> A3 · Encounter · <b>Scenario:</b> TC-15/S07</p><p><b>Typed medication questions with one right answer: why held, held now, stopped, given once (Hospital; NH variants)</b></p><p><b>Tickets:</b> TFA-92593 Ask AI (ready for qa)</p><p><b>Result:</b> Pass from <code>scripts/oracle.mjs</code> on the saved evidence (<code>units/U36.verdict.json</code>), unit U36. Agent: 69 turns, 385 s, $0.43.</p><p><b>Plan:</b> unit U36 (#36, ready-for-qa, live AI (Save Note / Save &amp; Extract / Ask AI)) — Pre-Round Ask: typed medication questions. Its Alvarez rows differ from every other Ask part's same-named patients.</p><p><b>Checked by Quinn's runner</b> (<code>ledger.md</code> #36, U36; checked: yes): <b>Blocked → runner fix</b> — GOAL starts with 'Navigate to &lt;chart URL&gt;' right after START opened /rounding → beforeunload ('leave site?') while the list's on-load writes were pending. Prompt: open the GOAL's first URL directly. Re-run below</p><p><b>Checked by Quinn's runner</b> (<code>ledger.md</code> #36b; checked: yes): <b>Pass</b> — 2nd run: 5/7, budget ran out on dev (maxSteps 56→80); 3rd run 7/7: why held / held now / stopped / given once answered from the tracker, both modes (e.g. 'not currently on lisinopril… held since Sep 29 for soft BP')</p>","environment":"default","setup":[],"teardown":[],"history":[],"retries":[],"breadcrumbs":[["TC-15 Ask AI","S07 Typed medication questions with one right answer: why held, held now, stopped, given once (Hospital…"]],"retry":false,"titlePath":[],"retriesCount":0,"attachments":[{"link":{"id":"b968413357d7e9ccc71b5caea4d497bc","originalFileName":"b5c60e1a-5610-4036-b3f9-f2cb68d770c2-attachment.txt","ext":".txt","name":"page snapshot (accessibility tree)","contentType":"text/plain","used":true,"missed":false,"contentLength":5299},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"5907817d96135734b17f29bd0a6beb41","originalFileName":"67fcac17-3855-4054-b207-8084bc7281a1-attachment.png","ext":".png","contentType":"image/png","contentLength":82983,"name":"screenshot"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"d927a4a89f11a80c24376e6bd071e388","originalFileName":"1afe4a7c-d55f-4087-abeb-c699e6ad3ad5-attachment.txt","ext":".txt","contentType":"text/plain","contentLength":5275,"name":"page snapshot (accessibility tree)"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"id":"93d77cd22c8abb637ad8952a35363eca","originalFileName":"f767f1ba-752e-4df5-b638-7b3d3808c33d-attachment.png","ext":".png","name":"screenshot","contentType":"image/png","used":true,"missed":false,"contentLength":84935},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"id":"2f27f89459c27e5ed4b1ecf773c849bb","originalFileName":"a3d6270e-8fd1-4e16-91cd-a0b6bdd8a4bc-attachment.txt","ext":".txt","name":"page snapshot (accessibility tree)","contentType":"text/plain","used":true,"missed":false,"contentLength":5213},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"id":"4027664e79a6e7dc7aa3f2261a427f4e","originalFileName":"c259bf26-13cb-405c-812e-32a72484a6f0-attachment.png","ext":".png","name":"screenshot","contentType":"image/png","used":true,"missed":false,"contentLength":81617},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"f116ede2bb0a943ec93502c006c23